(2) INDUCTIVE TOWER test: does inserting runner n into a covering (n-1)-family give a
    clean lower-bound recursion M_n >= g(M_{n-1})? (vertex insertion: M can only DECREASE)
  n=6: cov-min(n-1)=0.23810 [0;4,5] -> cov-min(n)=0.19355 [0;5,6]; ratio=0.8129
  n=7: cov-min(n-1)=0.19355 [0;5,6] -> cov-min(n)=0.16279 [0;6,7]; ratio=0.8411
  n=8: cov-min(n-1)=0.16279 [0;6,7] -> cov-min(n)=0.14035 [0;7,8]; ratio=0.8622
  n=9: cov-min(n-1)=0.14035 [0;7,8] -> cov-min(n)=0.12329 [0;8,9]; ratio=0.8784
  n=10: cov-min(n-1)=0.12329 [0;8,9] -> cov-min(n)=0.10989 [0;9,10]; ratio=0.8913

(3) is 'covering => M >= n/Phi6' a TREE fact or a METRIC fact? The Farey tree ORGANIZES
    the M-spectrum (1/14 < 3/41 < 2/27 < 14/183 < 1/13, mediants), but WHICH families are
    covering (land >= 14/183) is metric -- the tree gives the VALUES' arithmetic, not the
    lower bound. Vertex-insertion M_n <= M_{n-1} (peeling) = the balance, undershoots multi-killer.
VERDICT probe: the CF tower [0;n-1,n] is the DEEP WELL's clean structure (a value tower),
not a lower-bound proof over all covering families -- same split as Delsarte/tournament.
